message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Memory Operations in MCP Agent Ecosystems: an Operation Taxonomy, an Evaluation Protocol, and a Reference Implementation"
abstract: >-
  Proposes a taxonomy of six agent-memory operations defined by pre/postconditions and
  observable evidence, an evaluation protocol with ten task families and a machine-validated
  report format, and a reference implementation as public MCP servers. This release adds the
  first two protocol runs: two memory servers measured on ten task families with three
  repetitions per family, per-operation profiles that are read side by side rather than ranked,
  and comparison tables generated from the two validated report files. Token and cost metrics
  are null by construction, because no model is in the loop; the claim ledger states explicitly
  what is not confirmed.
type: article
